  "second_failure": "The separate unprivileged CHILD-DOUBLE-LOSS run passed the scope boundary but failed warm GX startup because Probe.env omitted TMPDIR, exposing a directory owned by host UID 0. The warm and cold GX subprocesses now share the experiment\u2019s existing private work directory. No product or billing criterion changed.",
  "reproduction": {
    "primary": "bin/gx-acceptance run all --case P2A-01; bin/gx-acceptance run hardening --case CHILD-DOUBLE-LOSS. Each public archive includes exact commands.json, environment.json and manifests.",
    "supplemental": "<python> supplemental.py <staged-checkout-with-.venv-and-vendor> <new-private-work> <clash>. Test with the owning host UID and a second unprivileged host UID.",
    "topology": "<python> topology.py <checkout> <writable-work> <clash> outer. In these runs, the second process ran as host UID/GID 65534, mapped to UID 0 inside unshare. The fixture stayed on loopback."
  },
